<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="7c0f2024">&lt;p&gt;
    The output of this task will be the development of a model quantifying potential financial and non-financial benefits.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    There are a number of ways to quantify a benefit. There is generally a need to obtain external data or evidence to help
    quantification, when there is limited internal experience of a specific type of innovation. Five approaches to obtain
    the data or evidence:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Detailed evidence, e.g. from existing systems&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Modeling or simulation, mainly in transactional or operational areas&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Benchmarking with ‘best practices’ in the industry&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Reference sites where similar changes have been made&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Pilot implementations to test the new way of working on a small scale
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="5db68390"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="825cacba">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        External benchmarking should be used to challenge old ways and spark new ideas. Being able to compare specific
        metrics against industry norms and leading practice can help reconfirm or stretch productivity assumptions.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Care should be taken to ensure that benefits that may be related to another existing or future planned program are
        not considered to avoid double counting.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        It is likely that in order to calculate the potential savings, it will be necessary to build a spreadsheet model
        that compares the future operating costs with the baseline operating costs and then shows how the benefits are
        phased over the lifecycle of the program. The structure of such a model is likely to vary depending on the size,
        scope and complexity of the program and therefore a generic template is not included within the toolkit.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="f99e9bd4"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="6b1fa391">To tie together program or project benefits with any foreseen risks and costs and set a realistic timeline for the
realization of benefits.</attribute>
<attribute name="alternatives" nodeId="e4c01181"></attribute>
